{
  "feature_instruction": "The Order Management feature handles the complete lifecycle of a customer order, from creation and payment processing to status updates and history viewing. It integrates with the `product-management-core` feature to retrieve product details and update stock, and with the pre-scaffolded `payment` foundation feature to process payments.\n\n## Order Creation Flow\n1.  **`OrderController.createOrder(CreateOrderRequest request, @CurrentUser Integer userId)`**: This endpoint receives a `CreateOrderRequest` from the authenticated user. It extracts the `userId` from the security context.\n2.  **`OrderService.createOrder(CreateOrderRequest request, Integer userId)`**: The service layer orchestrates the order creation:\n    a.  It validates the `CreateOrderRequest`, ensuring all `OrderItemRequest` objects have valid `productId` and `quantity`.\n    b.  For each `OrderItemRequest`, it retrieves the `Product` and `ProductVariant` (if applicable) from the `product-management-core` feature using `ProductService.getProductById(Long productId)` and `ProductService.getProductVariantById(Long variantId)` (assuming a variant ID is provided in `OrderItemRequest`). It verifies stock availability.\n    c.  It calculates the total amount of the order.\n    d.  It creates a new `Order` entity with `PENDING` status, associating it with the `userId` and the provided shipping details.\n    e.  It creates `OrderItem` entities for each item in the request, linking them to the `Order`.\n    f.  It calls the pre-scaffolded `PaymentService.createOrder(new CreatePaymentRequest(amount, \"INR\", \"order_\" + order.getId()))` to initiate a payment. The `PaymentService` returns a `PaymentOrderResponse`.\n    g.  If the payment initiation is successful, it saves the `Order` and `OrderItem` entities to the database via `OrderRepository.save()` and `OrderItemRepository.saveAll()`.\n    h.  It updates the stock for each `ProductVariant` by calling `ProductService.updateProductVariantStock(Long variantId, Integer quantityChange)` with a negative `quantityChange`.\n    i.  It returns an `OrderResponse` containing the created order details and payment information.\n    j.  If any product is out of stock or the payment fails, it throws an `IllegalStateException` or `PaymentGatewayException` respectively.\n\n## Order History and Details\n1.  **`OrderController.getMyOrders(@CurrentUser Integer userId)`**: Retrieves a list of orders for the authenticated user.\n2.  **`OrderController.getOrderById(Long orderId, @CurrentUser Integer userId)`**: Retrieves details for a specific order belonging to the authenticated user.\n3.  **`OrderService.getOrdersByUserId(Integer userId)`**: Fetches all orders for a given `userId` from `OrderRepository.findByUserIdOrderByCreatedAtDesc()` and maps them to `OrderHistoryItemDto`.\n4.  **`OrderService.getOrderByIdAndUserId(Long orderId, Integer userId)`**: Fetches a specific order by `orderId` and `userId` from `OrderRepository.findByIdAndUserId()` and maps it to `OrderResponse`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the order is not found or does not belong to the user.\n\n## Admin Order Management\n1.  **`AdminOrderController.getAllOrders()`**: Retrieves all orders in the system.\n2.  **`AdminOrderController.getOrderById(Long orderId)`**: Retrieves details for any specific order.\n3.  **`AdminOrderController.updateOrderStatus(Long orderId, OrderStatus newStatus)`**: Updates the status of an order.\n4.  **`OrderService.getAllOrders()`**: Fetches all orders from `OrderRepository.findAll()` and maps them to `OrderHistoryItemDto`.\n5.  **`OrderService.getOrderById(Long orderId)`**: Fetches a specific order by `orderId` from `OrderRepository.findById()` and maps it to `OrderResponse`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the order is not found.\n6.  **`OrderService.updateOrderStatus(Long orderId, OrderStatus newStatus)`**: Updates the status of an order. It retrieves the order using `OrderRepository.findById()`, updates its `orderStatus`, and saves it. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the order is not found.\n\n## Data Models and DTOs\n-   **`Order`**: The JPA entity representing an order, including `userId`, `shippingAddress`, `shippingMethod`, `orderStatus`, `totalAmount`, and a list of `OrderItem`s.\n-   **`OrderItem`**: The JPA entity for a single item within an order, referencing a `Product` and storing `quantity`, `unitPrice`, and `productVariantId`.\n-   **`OrderStatus`**: An enum defining possible states of an order (e.g., `PENDING`, `PROCESSING`, `SHIPPED`, `DELIVERED`, `CANCELLED`).\n-   **`ShippingMethod`**: An enum defining available shipping options (e.g., `HOME_DELIVERY`, `CLICK_AND_COLLECT`).\n-   **`CreateOrderRequest`**: DTO for incoming order creation requests, containing `List<OrderItemRequest>`, `shippingAddress`, `city`, `state`, `pincode`, and `shippingMethod`.\n-   **`OrderItemRequest`**: DTO for a single item within `CreateOrderRequest`, containing `productId`, `quantity`, and optional `productVariantId`.\n-   **`OrderResponse`**: DTO for outgoing order details, including all fields of `Order` and `OrderItem`s, along with payment details.\n-   **`OrderHistoryItemDto`**: A simplified DTO for displaying order summaries in a list, containing `orderId`, `orderDate`, `totalAmount`, and `orderStatus`.",
