  "feature_instruction": "The Event Management feature enables Prakash Stores to announce and manage in-store events like workshops or collection previews. It consists of a backend API for public viewing and admin-only CRUD operations, and corresponding data models and DTOs.\n\n**Event Model (`Event.java`)**\nThis JPA entity represents an event with fields for `id`, `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `location`, and `imageUrl`. The `eventDate` will be a `LocalDateTime` to store both date and time, and `imageUrl` will store a URL to an image hosted in the media gallery.\n\n**Event Repository (`EventRepository.java`)**\nThis Spring Data JPA repository provides standard CRUD operations for the `Event` entity. It will also include a custom query method `findByEventDateAfterOrderByEventDateAsc(LocalDateTime date)` to fetch upcoming events and `findByEventDateBeforeOrderByEventDateDesc(LocalDateTime date)` for past events.\n\n**Event Service (`EventService.java`)**\nThis service layer handles the core business logic for events. It injects `EventRepository` to interact with the database. All public methods will use `EventDto` for responses and `CreateEventRequest` for creation, ensuring a clean separation between the domain model and API contracts.\n\n1.  `EventDto createEvent(CreateEventRequest request)`:\n    *   Validates the `CreateEventRequest`. If `request.name` or `request.eventDate` are null, throw `IllegalArgumentException`.\n    *   Creates a new `Event` entity from the request data.\n    *   Saves the `Event` using `eventRepository.save()`.\n    *   Returns the saved `Event` mapped to an `EventDto`.\n\n2.  `EventDto getEventById(Long id)`:\n    *   Fetches an `Event` by its `id` using `eventRepository.findById()`.\n    *   If the event is not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n    *   Returns the `Event` mapped to an `EventDto`.\n\n3.  `List<EventDto> getAllEvents()`:\n    *   Fetches all `Event` entities using `eventRepository.findAll()`.\n    *   Maps each `Event` to an `EventDto` and returns a list.\n\n4.  `List<EventDto> getUpcomingEvents()`:\n    *   Fetches events with `eventDate` after the current time, ordered ascending by `eventDate` using `eventRepository.findByEventDateAfterOrderByEventDateAsc(LocalDateTime.now())`.\n    *   Maps each `Event` to an `EventDto` and returns a list.\n\n5.  `List<EventDto> getPastEvents()`:\n    *   Fetches events with `eventDate` before the current time, ordered descending by `eventDate` using `eventRepository.findByEventDateBeforeOrderByEventDateDesc(LocalDateTime.now())`.\n    *   Maps each `Event` to an `EventDto` and returns a list.\n\n6.  `EventDto updateEvent(Long id, CreateEventRequest request)`:\n    *   Finds the existing `Event` by `id` using `eventRepository.findById()`. If not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n    *   Updates the `Event` entity with data from the `CreateEventRequest`. If `request.name` or `request.eventDate` are null, throw `IllegalArgumentException`.\n    *   Saves the updated `Event` using `eventRepository.save()`.\n    *   Returns the updated `Event` mapped to an `EventDto`.\n\n7.  `void deleteEvent(Long id)`:\n    *   Checks if an `Event` with the given `id` exists using `eventRepository.existsById()`. If not, throws `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n    *   Deletes the `Event` using `eventRepository.deleteById()`.\n\n**Event DTOs (`EventDto.java`, `CreateEventRequest.java`)**\n`EventDto` is used for public API responses, containing `id`, `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `location`, and `imageUrl`. `CreateEventRequest` is used for creating and updating events, containing `name`, `description`, `eventDate`, `location`, and `imageUrl` with appropriate validation annotations.\n\n**Event Controller (`EventController.java`)**\nThis public REST controller exposes endpoints for retrieving event information. It injects `EventService`.\n\n1.  `GET /api/v1/events`: Returns a `List<EventDto>` of all events.\n2.  `GET /api/v1/events/upcoming`: Returns a `List<EventDto>` of upcoming events.\n3.  `GET /api/v1/events/past`: Returns a `List<EventDto>` of past events.\n4.  `GET /api/v1/events/{id}`: Returns an `EventDto` for a specific event by `id`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (handled by `GlobalExceptionHandler`) if not found, returning HTTP 404.\n\n**Admin Event Controller (`AdminEventController.java`)**\nThis admin-only REST controller provides CRUD capabilities for events. It injects `EventService`.\n\n1.  `POST /api/v1/admin/events`: Creates a new event. Takes `CreateEventRequest` as `@RequestBody`. Returns the created `EventDto` with HTTP 201. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` (handled by `GlobalExceptionHandler`) for invalid input, returning HTTP 400.\n2.  `PUT /api/v1/admin/events/{id}`: Updates an existing event. Takes `Long id` from path and `CreateEventRequest` as `@RequestBody`. Returns the updated `EventDto`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (handled by `GlobalExceptionHandler`) if not found, returning HTTP 404, or `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid input, returning HTTP 400.\n3.  `DELETE /api/v1/admin/events/{id}`: Deletes an event by `id`. Returns HTTP 204 No Content on success. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (handled by `GlobalExceptionHandler`) if not found, returning HTTP 404.\n4.  `GET /api/v1/admin/events`: Returns a `List<EventDto>` of all events. This is identical to the public endpoint but is secured for admin access.\n5.  `GET /api/v1/admin/events/{id}`: Returns an `EventDto` for a specific event by `id`. This is identical to the public endpoint but is secured for admin access. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (handled by `GlobalExceptionHandler`) if not found, returning HTTP 404.\n\n**Error Handling**\n`ResourceNotFoundException` will be thrown by `EventService` methods when an entity is not found, and `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid input. These will be caught by the `GlobalExceptionHandler` (from `shared-backend`) and translated into appropriate HTTP responses (404 Not Found and 400 Bad Request respectively).",
