  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A3A6D] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#E87A00] hover:bg-[#D46B00] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#E87A00]\n- Section bg: bg-white (odd sections) / bg-[#F5F5F5] (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#212121] leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature provides the frontend for the product catalog, allowing users to browse products, view details, filter by categories and brands, add items to the cart, and submit reviews. It consists of TypeScript types, service functions for API interaction, and React components for UI rendering.\n\n`frontend/src/types/product.ts` defines the data structures for `Product`, `Category`, `Brand`, and `ProductVariant` based on the `product-management-api` backend contracts. Similarly, `frontend/src/types/review.ts` defines the `Review` type based on `customer-features`.\n\n`frontend/src/services/productService.ts` and `frontend/src/services/reviewService.ts` are responsible for making API calls to the `product-management-api` and `customer-features` backends, respectively. These services will use the generated API client (`@/api/client`) to fetch data.\n\n`frontend/src/pages/ProductsPage.tsx` is the main entry point for the product catalog. It fetches a paginated list of products and available categories/brands using the generated service functions. It renders a `ProductFilterSidebar` for filtering and a `ProductGrid` to display the products. The `ProductGrid` iterates over the fetched products and renders a `ProductCard` for each. Each `ProductCard` will display the product's image, name, and price, and include a button to add the product to the cart. The price should be formatted in Indian Rupees (₹) using `toLocal