  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A3A6D] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#E87A00] hover:bg-[#D46B00] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#E87A00]\n- Section bg: bg-white (odd sections) / bg-[#F5F5F5] (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#212121] leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature implements the complete checkout flow for Prakash Stores, from displaying the cart contents to confirming an order. It leverages the pre-scaffolded cart framework (`useCart()`, `useCheckout()`) for managing cart state and orchestrating checkout steps, and interacts with the `order-management` backend feature for creating orders and fetching order details. All monetary values are displayed in Indian Rupees (₹) using the `en-IN` locale.\n\n### `frontend/src/types/order.ts`\nThis file defines the TypeScript interfaces for `Order`, `OrderItem`, `CreateOrderRequest`, and `OrderItemRequest`, mirroring the backend `order-management` feature's DTOs. These types ensure strong typing throughout the frontend checkout process.\n\n### `frontend/src/services/orderService.ts`\nThis service provides functions to interact with the `order-management` backend API. It exports `createOrder(request: CreateOrderRequest): Promise<OrderResponse>` to place a new order and `getOrderById(orderId: Long): Promise<OrderResponse>` to retrieve details of a specific order. It uses the `@/api/client` for making authenticated API calls.\n\n### `frontend/src/pages/CartPage.tsx`\nThis page renders the user's shopping cart. It uses the `CartView` component to display the cart items and summary. The page's primary responsibility is to fetch cart data using `useCart()` and pass it down to `CartView`. It provides a clear call to action to proceed to checkout.\n\n### `frontend/src/pages/CheckoutPage.tsx`\nThis page orchestrates the multi-step checkout process. It utilizes the `useCheckout()` hook from the cart framework to manage the checkout steps (e.g., Shipping, Payment, Review). The `CheckoutSteps` component is used to render the current step. Upon successful payment and order creation, it navigates the user to the `OrderConfirmationPage`.\n\n### `frontend/src/pages/OrderConfirmationPage.tsx`\nThis page displays a summary of a successfully placed order. It retrieves the `orderId` from the URL parameters and uses `orderService.getOrderById(orderId)` to fetch the order details. The page presents the order number, total amount, shipping address, and a list of purchased items, all formatted for the Indian locale.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/cart/CartView.tsx`\nThis component is the main container for displaying the cart. It consumes `cartItems` and `totals` from `useCart()` and renders `CartItemCard` for each item and `CartSummary` for the financial breakdown. It includes a section for a clear call to action to proceed to checkout.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/cart/CartItemCard.tsx`\nThis component displays a single item in the shopping cart. It receives a `CartItem` as a prop and provides controls to increment/decrement the quantity using `useCart().setItemQuantity(id, newQty, variantKey)` and to remove the item using `useCart().removeItem(id, variantKey)`. Item prices are displayed in Indian Rupees.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/cart/CartSummary.tsx`\nThis component displays the financial summary of the cart, including subtotal, adjustments (if any), and the total amount. It retrieves `totals` from `useCart()`. It also includes a prominent button to navigate to the checkout page. All amounts are formatted in Indian Rupees.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/checkout/CheckoutSteps.tsx`\nThis component is responsible for rendering the appropriate checkout step based on the `currentStep` provided by `useCheckout()`. It conditionally renders `ShippingAddressForm` and `PaymentStep` components. It also manages navigation between steps using `useCheckout().nextStep()` and `useCheckout().prevStep()`.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/checkout/ShippingAddressForm.tsx`\nThis form allows the user to enter their shipping address details (shippingAddress, city, state, pincode) and select a shipping method. It integrates with `useCheckout()` to update the checkout state with the entered shipping information. Validation is performed before allowing the user to proceed to the next step.\n\n### `frontend/src/components/checkout/PaymentStep.tsx`\nThis component handles the payment process. It gathers the necessary order details from `useCart().cartItems` and `useCart().totals.total`, along with the shipping information from `useCheckout().checkoutState`. It then constructs a `CreateOrderRequest` and calls `orderService.createOrder(request)` to place the order. Upon successful order creation, it calls `useCart().clearCart()` and navigates to the `OrderConfirmationPage`. It also integrates with the pre-scaffolded `PaymentService` (via the backend's `order-management` feature) to process payments. Error handling for payment failures is included, displaying appropriate messages to the user."
