{
  "feature_instruction": "The Product Management API feature provides both public-facing endpoints for browsing products, categories, and brands, and admin-only endpoints for managing these entities. It consists of two controllers: `ProductController` for public access and `AdminProductController` for administrative CRUD operations. All business logic and data persistence are delegated to the `product-management-core` feature's `ProductService`. This feature defines several DTOs (`ProductDto`, `CategoryDto`, `BrandDto`, `ProductVariantDto`, `ProductFilterParams`, `CreateProductRequest`, `UpdateProductRequest`) to structure the data exchanged with clients.\n\n### ProductController\nThis controller handles public requests for product information. It injects `ProductService` to retrieve data.\n\n1.  `getAllProducts(ProductFilterParams filterParams, Pageable pageable)`: \n    - Calls `productService.getAllProducts(filterParams, pageable)`.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing a `Page<ProductDto>` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n2.  `getProductById(Long productId)`: \n    - Calls `productService.getProductById(productId)`.\n    - If `productService.getProductById` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing a `ProductDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n3.  `getAllCategories()`: \n    - Calls `productService.getAllCategories()`.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing a `List<CategoryDto>` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n4.  `getCategoryById(Long categoryId)`: \n    - Calls `productService.getCategoryById(categoryId)`.\n    - If `productService.getCategoryById` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing a `CategoryDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n5.  `getAllBrands()`: \n    - Calls `productService.getAllBrands()`.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing a `List<BrandDto>` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n6.  `getBrandById(Long brandId)`: \n    - Calls `productService.getBrandById(brandId)`.\n    - If `productService.getBrandById` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing a `BrandDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n\n### AdminProductController\nThis controller handles administrative requests for creating, updating, and deleting products, categories, and brands. It injects `ProductService` to perform these operations.\n\n1.  `createProduct(CreateProductRequest request)`: \n    - Validates the `CreateProductRequest` using `@Valid`.\n    - Calls `productService.createProduct(request)`.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing the created `ProductDto` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n2.  `updateProduct(Long productId, UpdateProductRequest request)`: \n    - Validates the `UpdateProductRequest` using `@Valid`.\n    - Calls `productService.updateProduct(productId, request)`.\n    - If `productService.updateProduct` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing the updated `ProductDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n3.  `deleteProduct(Long productId)`: \n    - Calls `productService.deleteProduct(productId)`.\n    - If `productService.deleteProduct` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` with no content and HTTP status 204 No Content.\n4.  `createCategory(CategoryDto categoryDto)`: \n    - Validates the `CategoryDto` using `@Valid`.\n    - Calls `productService.createCategory(categoryDto)`.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing the created `CategoryDto` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n5.  `updateCategory(Long categoryId, CategoryDto categoryDto)`: \n    - Validates the `CategoryDto` using `@Valid`.\n    - Calls `productService.updateCategory(categoryId, categoryDto)`.\n    - If `productService.updateCategory` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing the updated `CategoryDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n6.  `deleteCategory(Long categoryId)`: \n    - Calls `productService.deleteCategory(categoryId)`.\n    - If `productService.deleteCategory` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` with no content and HTTP status 204 No Content.\n7.  `createBrand(BrandDto brandDto)`: \n    - Validates the `BrandDto` using `@Valid`.\n    - Calls `productService.createBrand(brandDto)`.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing the created `BrandDto` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n8.  `updateBrand(Long brandId, BrandDto brandDto)`: \n    - Validates the `BrandDto` using `@Valid`.\n    - Calls `productService.updateBrand(brandId, brandDto)`.\n    - If `productService.updateBrand` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` containing the updated `BrandDto` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n9.  `deleteBrand(Long brandId)`: \n    - Calls `productService.deleteBrand(brandId)`.\n    - If `productService.deleteBrand` throws `ResourceNotFoundException`, the controller will return a 404 Not Found response.\n    - Returns a `ResponseEntity` with no content and HTTP status 204 No Content.\n\n### DTOs\n- `ProductDto`: Represents the public view of a product, including its name, description, price, image URL, category, brand, variants, and active status.\n- `CategoryDto`: Represents a product category with an ID, name, and description.\n- `BrandDto`: Represents a product brand with an ID, name, and description.\n- `ProductVariantDto`: Represents a specific variant of a product, including size, color, SKU, stock, additional price, and image URL.\n- `ProductFilterParams`: Used to encapsulate query parameters for filtering products (category ID, brand ID, search term, min/max price).\n- `CreateProductRequest`: Used for creating new products, containing all necessary fields for product and variant creation.\n- `UpdateProductRequest`: Used for updating existing products, containing all necessary fields for product and variant updates.\n\nAll controllers will handle `ResourceNotFoundException` by returning a `404 Not Found` HTTP status, and other exceptions will be handled by a global exception handler (from `shared-backend`) returning a `500 Internal Server Error`.",
