  "feature_instruction": "The Product Management API feature provides a comprehensive set of endpoints for managing and browsing products, categories, and brands for Prakash Stores. It consists of two main controllers: `ProductController` for public access to product catalog data, and `AdminProductController` for administrative CRUD operations. All business logic is delegated to the `product-management-core` feature's `ProductService`.\n\n### ProductController.java\nThis controller handles public-facing requests for product information. It exposes endpoints for retrieving paginated lists of products, individual product details, and lists of categories and brands. All methods in this controller are read-only and accessible to unauthenticated users.\n\n1.  `getAllProducts(ProductFilterParams filterParams, Pageable pageable)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<Page<ProductDto>> getAllProducts(@ModelAttribute ProductFilterParams filterParams, @PageableDefault(size = 10, sort = \"name\") Pageable pageable)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.getAllProducts(filterParams, pageable)`.\n        3.  Return the `Page<ProductDto>` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: None specific; `ProductService` handles internal errors.\n\n2.  `getProductById(Long productId)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<ProductDto> getProductById(@PathVariable Long productId)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.getProductById(productId)`.\n        3.  Return the `ProductDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if `productService.getProductById` returns null or throws an exception, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found.\n\n3.  `getAllCategories()`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<List<CategoryDto>> getAllCategories()`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.getAllCategories()`.\n        3.  Return the `List<CategoryDto>` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: None specific.\n\n4.  `getCategoryById(Long categoryId)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<CategoryDto> getCategoryById(@PathVariable Long categoryId)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.getCategoryById(categoryId)`.\n        3.  Return the `CategoryDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if `productService.getCategoryById` returns null or throws an exception, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found.\n\n5.  `getAllBrands()`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<List<BrandDto>> getAllBrands()`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.getAllBrands()`.\n        3.  Return the `List<BrandDto>` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: None specific.\n\n6.  `getBrandById(Long brandId)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<BrandDto> getBrandById(@PathVariable Long brandId)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.getBrandById(brandId)`.\n        3.  Return the `BrandDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if `productService.getBrandById` returns null or throws an exception, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found.\n\n### AdminProductController.java\nThis controller provides administrative endpoints for creating, updating, and deleting products, categories, and brands. All methods in this controller require administrative authentication.\n\n1.  `createProduct(CreateProductRequest request)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<ProductDto> createProduct(@RequestBody @Valid CreateProductRequest request)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.createProduct(request)`.\n        3.  Return the created `ProductDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid request data, resulting in HTTP status 400 Bad Request.\n\n2.  `updateProduct(Long productId, UpdateProductRequest request)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<ProductDto> updateProduct(@PathVariable Long productId, @RequestBody @Valid UpdateProductRequest request)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.updateProduct(productId, request)`.\n        3.  Return the updated `ProductDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the product is not found, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid request data, resulting in HTTP status 400 Bad Request.\n\n3.  `deleteProduct(Long productId)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<Void> deleteProduct(@PathVariable Long productId)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.deleteProduct(productId)`.\n        3.  Return a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 204 No Content.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the product is not found, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found.\n\n4.  `createCategory(CategoryDto categoryDto)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<CategoryDto> createCategory(@RequestBody @Valid CategoryDto categoryDto)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.createCategory(categoryDto)`.\n        3.  Return the created `CategoryDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid request data or if a category with the same name already exists, resulting in HTTP status 400 Bad Request.\n\n5.  `updateCategory(Long categoryId, CategoryDto categoryDto)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<CategoryDto> updateCategory(@PathVariable Long categoryId, @RequestBody @Valid CategoryDto categoryDto)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.updateCategory(categoryId, categoryDto)`.\n        3.  Return the updated `CategoryDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the category is not found, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid request data or if a category with the same name already exists, resulting in HTTP status 400 Bad Request.\n\n6.  `deleteCategory(Long categoryId)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<Void> deleteCategory(@PathVariable Long categoryId)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.deleteCategory(categoryId)`.\n        3.  Return a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 204 No Content.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the category is not found, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found. Throws `IllegalStateException` if the category is still associated with products, resulting in HTTP status 409 Conflict.\n\n7.  `createBrand(BrandDto brandDto)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<BrandDto> createBrand(@RequestBody @Valid BrandDto brandDto)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.createBrand(brandDto)`.\n        3.  Return the created `BrandDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 201 Created.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid request data or if a brand with the same name already exists, resulting in HTTP status 400 Bad Request.\n\n8.  `updateBrand(Long brandId, BrandDto brandDto)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<BrandDto> updateBrand(@PathVariable Long brandId, @RequestBody @Valid BrandDto brandDto)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.updateBrand(brandId, brandDto)`.\n        3.  Return the updated `BrandDto` wrapped in a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 200 OK.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the brand is not found, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found. Throws `IllegalArgumentException` for invalid request data or if a brand with the same name already exists, resulting in HTTP status 400 Bad Request.\n\n9.  `deleteBrand(Long brandId)`:\n    -   **Signature**: `ResponseEntity<Void> deleteBrand(@PathVariable Long brandId)`\n    -   **Logic**:\n        1.  Inject `ProductService`.\n        2.  Call `productService.deleteBrand(brandId)`.\n        3.  Return a `ResponseEntity` with HTTP status 204 No Content.\n    -   **Error Cases**: Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the brand is not found, resulting in HTTP status 404 Not Found. Throws `IllegalStateException` if the brand is still associated with products, resulting in HTTP status 409 Conflict.\n\n### DTOs\nThe DTOs (`ProductDto`, `CategoryDto`, `BrandDto`, `ProductVariantDto`, `ProductFilterParams`, `CreateProductRequest`, `UpdateProductRequest`) define the data structures for requests and responses. They include necessary validation annotations for data integrity. These DTOs are used by both controllers to communicate with the `ProductService` and to expose data to the frontend.",
